cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software (below) and the paper in preferred-citation."
type: software
title: "Lignin_Forward_Gen: a forward generator for lignin linkage distributions"
abstract: >-
  A minimal, transparent forward generator that predicts the native lignin
  inter-unit linkage inventory (beta-O-4, beta-5, beta-beta, beta-1, 5-5, 4-O-5)
  from monomer composition (S/G ratio and H fraction) alone. Lignin is built one
  coupling at a time: at each step one coupling is drawn with probability
  proportional to its constant times the number of eligible pairs; there is no
  clock and no rate constants, so only the ratios of the constants matter (it is
  not a kinetic Monte Carlo model). Three rules of radical coupling apply: only
  phenolic chain ends accept an incoming monomer, beta-beta forms only between two
  monomers, and beta-1 needs an acceptor already in a beta-O-4. Seven dimensionless
  constants are calibrated by Nelder-Mead on sixty native lignins from thirteen
  sources (quantitative 13C and HSQC NMR), each paper weighted equally, and
  validated by leave-one-sample-out and leave-one-source-out cross-validation;
  eleven further lignins are used for validation only. The linkage distribution
  emerges from the coupling rules and supply rather than being imposed as a target.
